                                            Divide and Conquer



D&C algorithms are recursive algorithms
1. Figure out the base case,this should be the simplest possible one
2. Divide or decrease your problem until it becomes the base case

Quick Sort:-
1. Pick an element from the array, this element is called the PIVOT
2. Partitioning: Pick elements smaller and larger from pivot

Now you have pivot, subarray of larger element than pivot, subarray fo smaller element than pivot
Call this partitioning recussively
Avg case: O(nlogn) Worst case: O(n*n)

Performance of quick sort heavily depends on the pivot you choose
Normally, in binary and linear search, the constant doesn't make much difference
But in quick and merge sort, quicksort has a smaller constant than merge sort, so if both of em has O(nlogn), qs is faster
